{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 10: a two-stage ageing chain of rookies and veterans. Rookies produce little and take veterans' time to mentor, so a hiring push lowers output first. Starts in balance with 100 veterans. }
Base Hiring=
	1.24
	~	person/month
	~	Hiring that replaces leavers: 1 veteran and 0.24 rookies a month.
	|
Push Size=
	20
	~	person/month
	~	Extra hiring rate during the push.
	|
Push Start=
	6
	~	month
	~	|
Push Duration=
	3
	~	month
	~	Twenty extra a month for three months: 60 extra hires, a 60% expansion.
	|
Hiring=
	Base Hiring + Push Size * PULSE(Push Start, Push Duration)
	~	person/month
	~	|
Rookies= INTEG(
	Hiring - Assimilation - Rookie Quits,
	6)
	~	person
	~	New people still learning the job.
	|
Assimilation Time=
	6
	~	month
	~	Average time for a rookie to become fully productive.
	|
Assimilation=
	Rookies / Assimilation Time
	~	person/month
	~	|
Rookie Quit Fraction=
	0.04
	~	1/month
	~	Rookies leave four times as often as veterans.
	|
Rookie Quits=
	Rookies * Rookie Quit Fraction
	~	person/month
	~	|
Veterans= INTEG(
	Assimilation - Veteran Quits,
	100)
	~	person
	~	Fully productive people.
	|
Veteran Quit Fraction=
	0.01
	~	1/month
	~	Average veteran tenure 100 months.
	|
Veteran Quits=
	Veterans * Veteran Quit Fraction
	~	person/month
	~	|
Productivity=
	10
	~	tasks/person/month
	~	Output of a veteran with no mentoring duties.
	|
Rookie Productivity=
	0.2
	~	dmnl
	~	A rookie's output as a fraction of a veteran's.
	|
Mentoring Load=
	0.3
	~	dmnl
	~	Veteran time spent per rookie (person per person).
	|
Mentoring=
	Rookies * Mentoring Load
	~	person
	~	Veteran time taken up by mentoring.
	|
Effective Staff=
	Veterans - Mentoring + Rookies * Rookie Productivity
	~	person
	~	Staff in veteran equivalents.
	|
Output=
	Productivity * Effective Staff
	~	tasks/month
	~	|
Total Staff=
	Rookies + Veterans
	~	person
	~	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ month ~ |
FINAL TIME = 60 ~ month ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ month ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.0625 ~ month ~ |
